  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Commonwealth Climate Finance Access Hub</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Department for Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT) has been a long standing supporter of the Commonwealth Climate Finance Access Hub (CCFAH) since its inception at CHOGM in 2015.  AUD 2.5m over three grant agreements have been provided to support small and vulnerable states in the Commonwealth to address capacity gaps that hinder access to international sources of climate finance.  The new proposal will support an existing Indo-Pacific Regional Advisor and Tonga National advisor, and install new advisors for Nauru, Kiribati, Tuvalu, and Sri Lanka and establish a new role &#x2018;CCFAH Knowledge Officer&#x2019;</narrative>
  </description>
